se and prognosis of 132 patients with diabetic non ketotic hyperosmolar state</article-title><source>Diabete Metab</source><year>1994</year><volume>20</volume><fpage>43</fpage><lpage>48</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8056135</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zouvanis</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Pieterse</surname><given-names>AC</given-names></name><name><surname>Sefiel</surname><given-names>HC</given-names></name><name><surname>Joffe</surname><given-names>BI</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Clinical characteristics and outcome of hyperglycaemic emergencies in Johannesburg Africans</article-title><source>Diabet Med</source><year>1997</year><volume>14</volume><fpage>603</fpage><lpage>606</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9223400</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/(SICI)1096-9136(199707)14:7&#x0003c;603::AID-DIA406&#x0003e;3.0.CO;2-V</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>